   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the civil service law, in relation to transparency in health insurance claims data for public employers participating in the New York state health insurance program",
    "basePrintNo": "S3788",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3788-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §162, Civ Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3788\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the civil service law, in relation to\ntransparency in health insurance claims data for public employers\nparticipating in the New York state health insurance program\n\nPURPOSE:  To provide public employers participating in NYSHIP\ninformation relating to benefits, claims and premium payments on\nquarterly basis.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Requires the Department of Financial Services to disclose\nto all employers participating in NYSHIP information on a quarterly\nbasis relating to that employers utilization of benefits, claims,\npremium payments. Including, but not limited to claims paid by the\nmonth, broken out by medical and pharmacy, and a separate listing of\nclaims over $50,000 in compliance with the health insurance\nportability and accountability act of 1996.\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  Local governments and school districts participating\nin the New York State Health Insurance Program (NYSHIP) are often not\nprovided timely, meaningful claims information about their own claims\nand experience, even if they request it. This makes it difficult for\nthem to calculate current and future health care costs. This\nlegislation requires the Department of Financial Services to provide\nNYSHIP participants with information relating to benefits, claims and\npremium payments on a quarterly basis. The overall goal is to make\nNYSHIP more transparent for local governments and school districts\nparticipating in the program.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: 2012: S.7499-A - Rules\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately.\n\n",
